<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="66962" href="schedule/2016/fall/ACE/499/66962.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120168" href="schedule/2016/fall.xml">Fall 2016</term><subject id="ACE" href="schedule/2016/fall/ACE.xml">Agricultural and Consumer Economics</subject><course id="499" href="schedule/2016/fall/ACE/499.xml">Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>GR </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Econ &amp; Environ Input Output</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course teaches the theory and techniques of input-output analysis with hands-on experience in applications to economic and environmental issues.  Input-output measures linkages and the propagation of a (economic or environmental) shock across sectors and regions of an economy.  It is commonly used for economic impact analysis, transportation planning, disaster relief, energy forecasing, environmental analysis (pollution attribution) and social accounting models.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2016-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>22</roomNumber><buildingName>ACES Lib, Info &amp; Alum Ctr</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Dall'Erba" firstName="S">Dall'Erba, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>